  "question": {
    "text": "Two wires of diameter 0.25 cm, one made of steel and other made of brass are loaded as shown in figure. The unloaded length of steel wire is 1.5 m&nbsp;and that of brass wire is 1.0 m. Young's modulus of steel is 2.0 × 10<sup>11</sup>&nbsp;and Young's modulus &nbsp;of Brass&nbsp;0.91 × 10<sup>11</sup> Pa. The elongations of steel and brass wires are respectively<br />\r<br />\r<img alt=\"\" src=\"assets\\qt0025_7d6cef6b2856.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%; object-fit:contain\" style=\"width: 147px; height: 166px;\" />"
  },
